{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural","type":"ConceptScheme","prefLabel":{"es":"Objeto geomorfológico natural","en":"Geomorphological natural feature"},"publisher":{"id":"https://www.igme.es/"},"license":{"id":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"},"hasTopConcept":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/base-de-montaña","prefLabel":{"es":"base de montaña","en":"mountainbase"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una montaña constituido por una falda o cuña coluvial, firme o aproximadamente cóncava, situada al pie de las pendientes.","en":"A geomorphologic component of mountains consisting of the strongly to slightly concave colluvial apron or wedge at the bottom of mountain slopes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/base-del-talud","prefLabel":{"es":"base del talud","en":"base slope"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por una pendiente cóncava lineal (perpendicular al contorno) que, independientemente de la pendiente lateral, forma un saliente o cuña al pie de una colina, dominado por procesos coluviales y de lavado de la pendiente y por la deposición de sedimentos","en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of the concave to linear slope (perpendicular to the contour) which, regardless of the lateral shape, is an area that forms an apron or wedge at the bottom of a hillside dominated by colluvial and slope wash processes and sediments"}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cara-desnuda","prefLabel":{"es":"cara desnuda","en":"free face"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina o montaña constituido por un afloramiento de roca desnuda que suele ser más empinado que el ángulo de reposo, y que proporciona fragmentos de roca y otros sedimentos a la pendiente coluvial situada inmediatamente debajo; generalmente aparece en la ladera de menor pendiente y puede incluir una parte o la totalidad de una ladera divergente o una cuesta.","en":"A geomorphologic component of hills and mountains consisting of an outcrop of bare rock that sheds rock fragments and other sediments to, and commonly stands more steeply than the angle of repose of, the colluvial slope immediately below; most commonly found on shoulder and back slope positions, and can comprise part or all of a nose slope or side slope."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cima-de-montaña","prefLabel":{"es":"cima de montaña","en":"mountaintop"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una montaña constituido por el nivel relativamente más elevado y caracterizado por pendientes relativamente cortas y sencillas compuestas por roca desnuda, residuos o sedimentos coluviales transportados desde corta distancia.","en":"A geomorphologic component of mountains consisting of the uppermost, comparatively level or gently sloped area of mountains, characterized by relatively short, simple slopes composed of bare rock, residuum, or short-transport colluvial sediments."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colina","prefLabel":{"es":"colina","en":"hill"},"definition":{"es":"Término genérico que designa un área elevada de la superficie terrestre, que se alza entre 30 y 300 metros sobre las tierras bajas circundantes y que presenta generalmente una cumbre nominal en relación con sus laderas, una silueta redondeada bien definida y pendientes que superan en general el 15 por ciento.","en":"A generic term for an elevated area of the land surface, rising at least 30 metres to as much as 300 metres above surrounding lowlands, usually with a nominal summit area relative to bounding slopes, a well-defined, rounded outline and slopes that generally exceed 15 percent."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cresta","prefLabel":{"es":"cresta","en":"crest"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por unas laderas convexas (perpendiculares al contorno) que convergen para formar la parte superior, estrecha y generalmente lineal, de la colina, cordillera o tierra alta, hasta el punto de que apenas subsiste una cumbre; está dominada por los procesos de erosión, lavado de laderas y movimiento de masas, y por los sedimentos","en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of the convex slopes (perpendicular to the contour) that form the narrow, roughly linear top area of a hill, ridge, or other upland where shoulders have converged to the extent that little or no summit remains; dominated by erosion, slope wash and mass movement processes and sediments"}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cuesta","prefLabel":{"es":"cuesta","en":"side slope"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por un área de la ladera lateralmente plana que determina que las corrientes de agua sean predominantemente paralelas. Las curvas de nivel son en general rectas.","en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of a laterally planar area of a hillside, resulting in predominantly parallel overland water flow. Contour lines generally form straight lines."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/depresion","prefLabel":{"es":"depresión","en":"depression"},"definition":{"es":"Parte relativamente hundida de la superficie terrestre; especialmente, área baja rodeada de tierras más altas.","en":"Any relatively sunken part of the Earth's surface; especially a low-lying area surrounded by higher ground."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/forma-erosiva","prefLabel":{"es":"forma erosiva","en":"destructional feature"},"definition":{"es":"Forma de relieve que debe su origen, su forma, su posición o su carácter general a procesos de eliminación de material por erosión o meteorización (degradación) resultantes del desgaste de la superficie terrestre.","en":"Site of a landform that owes its origin, form, position, or general character to the removal of material by erosion and weathering (degradation) processes resulting from the wearing-down or away of the land surface."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/formacion-superficial","prefLabel":{"es":"formación superficial","en":"constructional feature"},"definition":{"es":"Forma de relieve que debe su origen, su forma, su posición o su carácter general a procesos de deposición (agradación), como la acumulación de sedimentos","en":"Site of a landform that owes its origin, form, position, or general character to depositional (aggradational) processes, such as the accumulation of sediment"}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/interfluvio","prefLabel":{"es":"interfluvio","en":"interfluve"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por el nivel relativamente más elevado o el área de pendiente más suave; las laderas pueden estrechar la zona superior o unirse para dar una forma muy convexa.","en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of the uppermost, comparatively level or gently sloped area of a hill; shoulders of back wearing hill slopes can narrow the upland or merge resulting in a strongly convex shape."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ladera","prefLabel":{"es":"ladera","en":"mountainflank"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una montaña caracterizado por pendientes muy largas y complejas con gradientes relativamente elevados y compuestas por mantos de sedimentos coluviales muy variados, afloramientos de roca y resaltes estructurales.","en":"A geomorphologic component of mountains characterized by very long, complex back slopes with comparatively high slope gradients and composed of highly-diverse colluvial sediment mantles, rock outcrops or structural benches."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ladera-divergente","prefLabel":{"es":"ladera divergente","en":"nose slope"},"definition":{"es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por un extremo saliente (generalmente un área convexa) de la ladera, que determina que las corrientes de agua sean predominantemente divergentes; las curvas de nivel son en general curvas convexas.","en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of the projecting end (laterally convex area) of a hillside, resulting in predominantly divergent overland water flow; contour lines generally form convex curves."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/llanura","prefLabel":{"es":"llanura","en":"plain"},"definition":{"es":"Área plana, grande o pequeña, de baja elevación; específicamente, una región extensa de tierra relativamente nivelada o poco ondulada, con pocas o ninguna irregularidad superficial, aunque a veces con una considerable pendiente, y generalmente con una baja elevación en relación con las áreas circundantes.","en":"Any flat area, large or small, at a low elevation; specifically an extensive region of comparatively smooth and level or gently undulaing land, having few or no prominent surface irregularities but sometimes having a considerable slope, and usually at a low elevation with reference to surrounding areas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/modelo-de-drenaje","prefLabel":{"es":"modelo de drenaje","en":"drainage pattern"},"definition":{"es":"Configuración o disposición de los cursos de agua en una zona, incluidos los barrancos o cursos canalizados de primer orden, los afluentes de orden superior y los cursos de agua principales.","en":"The configuration or arrangement of stream courses in an area, including gullies or first-order channelized flow areas, higher order tributaries, and main streams."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/montaña","prefLabel":{"es":"montaña","en":"mountain"},"definition":{"es":"Término genérico que designa un área elevada de la superficie terrestre, que se levanta más de 300 metros sobre las tierras bajas circundantes y presenta generalmente una cumbre definida en relación con sus laderas y pendientes que suelen ser empinadas (más del 25 por ciento), con o sin exposición considerable de roca desnuda.","en":"A generic term for an elevated area of the land surface, rising more than 300 metres above surrounding lowlands, usually with a nominal summit area relative to bounding slopes and generally with steep sides (greater than 25 percent slope) with or without considerable bare-rock exposed."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-degradativo","prefLabel":{"es":"objeto degradativo","en":"degradation feature"},"definition":{"es":"Objeto geomorfológico resultante del desgaste, y en general la reducción, de la superficie terrestre por procesos naturales de meteorización y erosión y que puede inducir procesos de transporte de sedimentos.","en":"A geomorphologic feature resulting from the wearing down or away, and the general lowering or reduction, of the Earth's surface by natural processes of weathering and erosion, and which may infer the processes of transportation of sediment."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-erosionado","prefLabel":{"es":"objeto erosionado","en":"erosional features"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie del terreno configurada por la acción de la erosión, sobre todo del agua corriente.","en":"A land surface shaped by the action of erosion, especially by running water."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-exhumado","prefLabel":{"es":"objeto exhumado","en":"exhumed feature"},"definition":{"es":"Forma del relieve, superficie geomorfológica o paleosuelo previmente enterrado que queda de nuevo expuesto por erosión del manto que lo cubría.","en":"Formerly buried landforms, geomorphologic surfaces, or paleosols that have been re-exposed by erosion of the covering mantle."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-fosilizado","prefLabel":{"es":"objeto fosilizado","en":"buried feature"},"definition":{"es":"Forma del relieve, superficie geomorfológica o paleosuelo cubierto por sedimentos más jóvenes.","en":"Landforms, geomorphologic surfaces, or paleosols covered by younger sediments."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-geomorfologico-natural","prefLabel":{"es":"objeto geomorfológico natural","en":"natural geomorphologic feature"},"definition":{"es":"Objeto geomorfológico producido por la dinámica natural.","en":"A geomorphologic feature produced by the natural dynamics."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-de-impacto","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos de impacto","en":"impact features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados con el impacto de objetos extraterrestres sobre la superficie terrestre.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to the impact of extraterrestrial material on the Earth's surface."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-eolicos","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos eólicos","en":"eolian features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a entornos dominados por el viento.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to wind-dominated environments."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arenas-eolicas-manto-eolico","prefLabel":{"es":"arenas eólicas; manto eólico","en":"aeolian sands; sand sheet"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito extenso de arena transportada por el viento.","en":"Extensive deposit of wind-transported sand."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-dunas-cordon-de-dunas","prefLabel":{"es":"campo de dunas; cordón de dunas","en":"dune field; dune ridge"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con acumulaciones de arena formadas por el viento.","en":"Area with sand accumulations formed by the wind."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-dunas-con-vegetacion","prefLabel":{"es":"campo de dunas con vegetación","en":"vegetated dune field"},"definition":{"es":"Campo de dunas parcial o totalmente estabilizado por vegetación.","en":"A dune field partially or totally stabilized by vegetation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-dunas-fosiles","prefLabel":{"es":"campo de dunas fósiles","en":"fossil dune field"},"definition":{"es":"Campo de dunas inactivas, fijadas y consolidadas.","en":"A field of inactive, fixed and consolidated dunes."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cresta-dunar","prefLabel":{"es":"cresta dunar","en":"dune crest"},"definition":{"es":"Línea más alta de una duna.","en":"The highest line of a dune."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cubetas-de-deflaccion","prefLabel":{"es":"cubetas de deflacción","en":"deflation hollows"},"definition":{"es":"Depresiones poco profundas excavadas por la acción del viento.","en":"Shallow depressions excavated by wind action."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas","prefLabel":{"es":"dunas","en":"dunes"},"definition":{"es":"Montículos de arena formados por acción eólica.","en":"Sand mounds formed by wind action."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/barjanes","prefLabel":{"es":"barjanes","en":"barchans"},"definition":{"es":"Dunas en forma de media luna con las puntas orientadas a sotavento.","en":"Crescent-shaped dunes with horns pointing downwind."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas-longitudinales","prefLabel":{"es":"dunas longitudinales","en":"longitudinal dunes"},"definition":{"es":"Dunas alargadas paralelas a la dirección del viento.","en":"Elongated dunes parallel to the wind direction."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas-parabolicas","prefLabel":{"es":"dunas parabólicas","en":"parabolic dunes"},"definition":{"es":"Dunas con forma de U o parábola abiertas en la dirección del viento.","en":"U-shaped or parabolic dunes open in the wind direction."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas-transversales","prefLabel":{"es":"dunas transversales","en":"transverse dunes"},"definition":{"es":"Dunas alargadas perpendiculares a la dirección del viento.","en":"Elongated dunes perpendicular to the wind direction."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas-trepadoras","prefLabel":{"es":"dunas trepadoras","en":"climbing dunes"},"definition":{"es":"Dunas que ascienden por una ladera empujadas por el viento.","en":"Dunes that climb up a slope driven by the wind."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/loess","prefLabel":{"es":"loess","en":"loess"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito de limo transportado y depositado por el viento.","en":"A deposit of silt transported and deposited by the wind."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ventifactos","prefLabel":{"es":"ventifactos","en":"ventifacts"},"definition":{"es":"Cantos con caras pulidas y facetas producidas por abrasión eólica.","en":"Pebbles with polished faces and facets produced by wind abrasion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/viento-dominante","prefLabel":{"es":"viento dominante","en":"prevailing wind"},"definition":{"es":"Dirección predominante del viento en una zona.","en":"Predominant wind direction in an area."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-geograficos-aluviales-y-fluviales","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos geográficos aluviales y fluviales","en":"alluvial and fluvial features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados predominantemente con corrientes de agua concentradas (corrientes canalizadas).","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms dominantly related to concentrated water flow (channel flow)."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/abanico-aluvial-de-baja-pendiente","prefLabel":{"es":"abanico aluvial de baja pendiente","en":"low-gradient alluvial fan"},"definition":{"es":"Abanico aluvial de gran extensión y baja pendiente.","en":"An alluvial fan of great extent and low gradient."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/albardon-dique-natural-levee","prefLabel":{"es":"albardón; dique natural; levée","en":"natural levee"},"definition":{"es":"Elevación alargada a lo largo de las márgenes de un río formada por desbordamiento.","en":"An elongated elevation along river margins formed by overbank flooding."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arista-o-divisoria-montanyosa","prefLabel":{"es":"arista o divisoria montañosa","en":"mountain ridge; divide"},"definition":{"es":"Cresta estrecha y aguda que separa cuencas hidrográficas en zonas montañosas.","en":"A narrow and sharp crest separating drainage basins in mountainous areas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/aristas-en-interfluvios","prefLabel":{"es":"aristas en interfluvios","en":"interfluve ridges"},"definition":{"es":"Crestas agudas que separan cauces fluviales adyacentes.","en":"Sharp ridges separating adjacent fluvial channels."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arroyada-en-regueros-permanentes-o-cambiantes","prefLabel":{"es":"arroyada en regueros, permanentes o cambiantes","en":"rill wash"},"definition":{"es":"Erosión superficial por flujo concentrado en pequeños surcos.","en":"Surface erosion by concentrated flow in small rills."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/banco-barra","prefLabel":{"es":"banco; barra","en":"bank; bar"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulación de sedimentos en el interior de un cauce fluvial.","en":"Sediment accumulation within a river channel."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/banco-barra-con-cicatrices-de-acrecion-lateral","prefLabel":{"es":"banco; barra con cicatrices de acreción lateral","en":"bar with lateral accretion scars"},"definition":{"es":"Barra fluvial con marcas visibles de crecimiento lateral.","en":"A fluvial bar with visible marks of lateral growth."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-terraza-en-niveles-solapados","prefLabel":{"es":"borde de terraza en niveles solapados","en":"overlapping terrace levels edge"},"definition":{"es":"Borde de terrazas fluviales que se solapan en su extensión lateral.","en":"Edge of fluvial terraces that overlap in their lateral extent."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cambio-brusco-de-pendiente-salto-de-agua-cascada","prefLabel":{"es":"cambio brusco de pendiente; salto de agua; cascada","en":"waterfall; cascade"},"definition":{"es":"Caída vertical o casi vertical del agua en un cauce fluvial.","en":"Vertical or near-vertical water drop in a river channel."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cambio-de-pendiente-rapidos","prefLabel":{"es":"cambio de pendiente; rápidos","en":"slope change; rapids"},"definition":{"es":"Zona de aumento de pendiente en un cauce fluvial con flujo turbulento.","en":"Zone of slope increase in a river channel with turbulent flow."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-principal-cauce-activo-en-grandes-rios-limite-del-lecho","prefLabel":{"es":"canal principal; cauce activo en grandes ríos; límite del lecho","en":"main channel; active bed limit"},"definition":{"es":"Cauce principal de un río o límite del lecho activo.","en":"Main channel of a river or limit of the active bed."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-temporal-o-de-avenida-brazo-de-corriente-aliviadero-chute","prefLabel":{"es":"canal temporal o de avenida, brazo de corriente, aliviadero; chute","en":"flood channel; chute"},"definition":{"es":"Canal que solo funciona durante crecidas o avenidas.","en":"A channel that only functions during floods."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/captura-fluvial","prefLabel":{"es":"captura fluvial","en":"river capture"},"definition":{"es":"Proceso por el cual un río desvía las aguas de otro al erosionar su divisoria.","en":"Process by which a river diverts the waters of another by eroding its divide."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/carcavas","prefLabel":{"es":"cárcavas","en":"gullies"},"definition":{"es":"Incisiones profundas y estrechas en materiales blandos producidas por erosión hídrica concentrada.","en":"Deep and narrow incisions in soft materials produced by concentrated water erosion."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-acarcavada","prefLabel":{"es":"área acarcavada","en":"gullied area"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con una alta densidad de cárcavas.","en":"An area with a high density of gullies."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cabecera-de-carcavas","prefLabel":{"es":"cabecera de cárcavas","en":"gully head"},"definition":{"es":"Parte superior de una cárcava donde se produce el retroceso erosivo.","en":"Upper part of a gully where erosional retreat occurs."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/carcavas-puntual","prefLabel":{"es":"cárcavas (puntual)","en":"gully (point feature)"},"definition":{"es":"Representación puntual de una cárcava individual.","en":"Point representation of an individual gully."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cauce-o-meandro-abandonado","prefLabel":{"es":"cauce o meandro abandonado","en":"abandoned channel; abandoned meander"},"definition":{"es":"Antiguo cauce o meandro que ya no es funcional.","en":"A former channel or meander that is no longer functional."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cauce-o-meandro-abandonado-temporalmente-inundado-oxbow","prefLabel":{"es":"cauce o meandro abandonado, temporalmente inundado; oxbow","en":"oxbow lake"},"definition":{"es":"Meandro abandonado que se inunda temporalmente formando un lago en herradura.","en":"An abandoned meander that temporarily floods forming an oxbow lake."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado","prefLabel":{"es":"collado; puerto; col","en":"pass; col"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso.","en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/confluencia-anomala-de-cauces","prefLabel":{"es":"confluencia anómala de cauces","en":"anomalous channel confluence"},"definition":{"es":"Unión de cauces fluviales con un ángulo o disposición inusual que sugiere control estructural.","en":"Junction of fluvial channels with an unusual angle or arrangement suggesting structural control."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-deyeccion-abanico-aluvial-con-pendiente-elevada","prefLabel":{"es":"cono de deyección; abanico aluvial con pendiente elevada","en":"alluvial fan; high-gradient fan"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito en forma de cono al pie de una montaña formado por corrientes torrenciales.","en":"Cone-shaped deposit at the foot of a mountain formed by torrential streams."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cuerda-o-divisoria-montanyosa-redondeada","prefLabel":{"es":"cuerda o divisoria montañosa redondeada","en":"rounded mountain divide"},"definition":{"es":"Divisoria de aguas con perfil redondeado y suave.","en":"A watershed divide with a rounded and gentle profile."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deposito-de-arroyada-aluvial-coluvial-relleno-de-vaguada","prefLabel":{"es":"depósito de arroyada; aluvial-coluvial; relleno de vaguada","en":"wash deposit; alluvial-colluvial fill"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito formado por arroyada difusa en vaguadas y laderas.","en":"Deposit formed by diffuse wash in thalwegs and slopes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrame-de-canal-crevasse-splay","prefLabel":{"es":"derrame de canal; crevasse splay","en":"crevasse splay"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito en abanico formado por la rotura del dique natural de un río.","en":"Fan-shaped deposit formed by the breach of a river natural levee."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/divisoria-de-aguas-poco-definida","prefLabel":{"es":"divisoria de aguas poco definida","en":"poorly defined watershed"},"definition":{"es":"Divisoria de aguas de trazado difuso y difícil de localizar con precisión.","en":"A watershed divide with a diffuse trace, difficult to locate precisely."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/erosion-lateral-zapamiento-socavamiento","prefLabel":{"es":"erosión lateral; zapamiento; socavamiento","en":"lateral erosion; undercutting"},"definition":{"es":"Erosión que actúa horizontalmente sobre las márgenes de un cauce.","en":"Erosion acting horizontally on the banks of a channel."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-fluvial","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe fluvial","en":"fluvial scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Talud vertical o subvertical tallado por la acción erosiva de un río.","en":"Vertical or subvertical slope carved by river erosive action."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-entre-25-100-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe entre 25-100 metros","en":"scarp 25-100 m"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe fluvial de entre 25 y 100 metros de altura.","en":"A fluvial scarp between 25 and 100 metres high."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-inferior-a-25-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe inferior a 25 metros","en":"scarp less than 25 m"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe fluvial de menos de 25 metros de altura.","en":"A fluvial scarp less than 25 metres high."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-superior-a-100-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe superior a 100 metros","en":"scarp over 100 m"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe fluvial de más de 100 metros de altura.","en":"A fluvial scarp over 100 metres high."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-o-borde-de-terraza-colgada-e-indicacion-de-cota-en-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe o borde de terraza colgada e indicación de cota en metros","en":"hanging terrace scarp with elevation in metres"},"definition":{"es":"Borde de una terraza fluvial colgada con indicación de su cota.","en":"Edge of a hanging fluvial terrace with elevation indication."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-o-borde-de-terraza-degradado","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe o borde de terraza degradado","en":"degraded terrace scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Borde de terraza fluvial suavizado por procesos erosivos.","en":"Fluvial terrace edge smoothed by erosional processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-rambla-torrencial","prefLabel":{"es":"fondo de rambla torrencial","en":"ephemeral stream bed"},"definition":{"es":"Lecho de un curso de agua torrencial con flujo intermitente.","en":"Bed of a torrential watercourse with intermittent flow."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-valle","prefLabel":{"es":"fondo de valle","en":"valley floor"},"definition":{"es":"Parte más baja y generalmente plana de un valle fluvial.","en":"The lowest and generally flat part of a fluvial valley."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-valle-colgado","prefLabel":{"es":"fondo de valle colgado","en":"hanging valley floor"},"definition":{"es":"Fondo plano de un valle colgado respecto al valle principal.","en":"Flat floor of a valley hanging above the main valley."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/garganta-canyon-fluvial-desfiladero","prefLabel":{"es":"garganta; cañón fluvial; desfiladero","en":"gorge; fluvial canyon"},"definition":{"es":"Valle muy estrecho y profundo con paredes verticales o subverticales.","en":"A very narrow and deep valley with vertical or subvertical walls."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hombrera","prefLabel":{"es":"hombrera; rellano","en":"shoulder; bench"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie subhorizontal que interrumpe una pendiente.","en":"A subhorizontal surface interrupting a slope."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/incision-dominada-por-sufusion-piping","prefLabel":{"es":"incisión dominada por sufusión; piping","en":"piping-dominated incision"},"definition":{"es":"Incisión del terreno dominada por procesos de erosión interna (piping).","en":"Terrain incision dominated by internal erosion processes (piping)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/incision-lineal-en-cuna-vaguada","prefLabel":{"es":"incisión lineal en cuna; vaguada","en":"wedge-shaped incision; thalweg"},"definition":{"es":"Incisión fluvial de perfil transversal en cuña o fondo plano poco desarrollado.","en":"Fluvial incision with a wedge-shaped or poorly developed flat-bottom cross section."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/incision-lineal-en-v-barranco","prefLabel":{"es":"incisión lineal en v; barranco","en":"V-shaped incision; ravine"},"definition":{"es":"Incisión fluvial de perfil transversal en forma de V.","en":"Fluvial incision with a V-shaped cross section."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/linea-de-drenaje-difusa","prefLabel":{"es":"línea de drenaje difusa","en":"diffuse drainage line"},"definition":{"es":"Línea de escorrentía sin cauce definido.","en":"A runoff line without a defined channel."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/llanura-de-inundacion","prefLabel":{"es":"llanura de inundación","en":"floodplain"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie plana adyacente a un río que se inunda periódicamente.","en":"A flat surface adjacent to a river that is periodically flooded."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/manantial","prefLabel":{"es":"manantial","en":"spring"},"definition":{"es":"Surgencia natural de agua subterránea en la superficie.","en":"Natural emergence of groundwater at the surface."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/perdida-de-drenaje","prefLabel":{"es":"pérdida de drenaje","en":"drainage loss"},"definition":{"es":"Punto donde un cauce fluvial pierde agua por infiltración.","en":"Point where a river channel loses water by infiltration."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/surgencia-por-sufusion-piping","prefLabel":{"es":"surgencia por sufusión; piping","en":"piping spring"},"definition":{"es":"Surgencia de agua producida por erosión interna del terreno.","en":"Water emergence produced by internal terrain erosion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza","en":"terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie plana elevada respecto al cauce actual, que representa un antiguo nivel del río.","en":"A flat surface elevated above the current channel, representing a former river level."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-erosiva","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza erosiva","en":"erosional terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Terraza tallada en la roca sin depósito aluvial significativo.","en":"A terrace carved into rock without significant alluvial deposit."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-no-ciclica-de-encajamiento-convergente","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza no cíclica (de encajamiento; convergente)","en":"non-cyclic terrace (entrenching; convergent)"},"definition":{"es":"Terraza formada por encajamiento progresivo sin relación con ciclos climáticos.","en":"Terrace formed by progressive entrenchment without relation to climatic cycles."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-travertinica","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza travertínica","en":"travertine terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Terraza formada por precipitación de carbonato cálcico (travertino).","en":"Terrace formed by calcium carbonate (travertine) precipitation."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/valle-colgado","prefLabel":{"es":"valle colgado","en":"hanging valley"},"definition":{"es":"Valle tributario cuyo fondo se encuentra a una cota más elevada que el valle principal.","en":"A tributary valley whose floor is at a higher elevation than the main valley."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/valle-o-vaguada-con-fondo-plano","prefLabel":{"es":"valle o vaguada con fondo plano","en":"flat-bottomed valley"},"definition":{"es":"Valle fluvial con fondo plano ocupado por depósitos aluviales.","en":"A fluvial valley with a flat bottom occupied by alluvial deposits."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-geograficos-karsticos-y-de-meteorizacion-quimica","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos geográficos kársticos y de meteorización química","en":"karst and chemical weathering features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve dominados por la disolución de minerales y, en general, por el drenaje subsuperficial.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms dominated by mineral dissolution, and commonly, subsurface drainage."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/aplanamiento-karstico-superficie-de-corrosion","prefLabel":{"es":"aplanamiento kárstico; superficie de corrosión","en":"karst planation surface"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie plana resultante de la disolución kárstica generalizada.","en":"A flat surface resulting from widespread karst dissolution."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-con-relieves-residuales-karsticos-hums","prefLabel":{"es":"área con relieves residuales kársticos; hums","en":"karst residual relief area; hums"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con abundantes relieves residuales kársticos.","en":"An area with abundant karst residual reliefs."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arenizacion-lehm-granitico","prefLabel":{"es":"arenización; lehm granítico","en":"arenization; granitic lehm"},"definition":{"es":"Meteorización que transforma la roca granítica en arena o lehm.","en":"Weathering that transforms granitic rock into sand or lehm."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/argilizaciones","prefLabel":{"es":"argilizaciones","en":"argillization"},"definition":{"es":"Transformación de minerales en arcilla por meteorización química.","en":"Transformation of minerals into clay by chemical weathering."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/berrocal","prefLabel":{"es":"berrocal","en":"boulder field; tor field"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con abundantes bolos graníticos residuales.","en":"An area with abundant residual granite boulders."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/bolos","prefLabel":{"es":"bolos","en":"boulders; corestones"},"definition":{"es":"Bloques redondeados residuales producidos por meteorización esferoidal.","en":"Rounded residual blocks produced by spheroidal weathering."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canyon-garganta-desfiladero","prefLabel":{"es":"cañón; garganta; desfiladero","en":"canyon; gorge"},"definition":{"es":"Valle muy profundo y estrecho con paredes verticales en terreno kárstico.","en":"A very deep and narrow valley with vertical walls in karst terrain."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/caolinizaciones","prefLabel":{"es":"caolinizaciones","en":"kaolinization"},"definition":{"es":"Transformación de feldespatos en minerales del grupo de la caolinita.","en":"Transformation of feldspars into kaolinite group minerals."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/carbonataciones","prefLabel":{"es":"carbonataciones","en":"carbonation"},"definition":{"es":"Formación de costras o acumulaciones de carbonato por precipitación.","en":"Formation of carbonate crusts or accumulations by precipitation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-ruiniforme","prefLabel":{"es":"cerro ruiniforme; caos de bloques","en":"ruiniform hill; block chaos"},"definition":{"es":"Relieve con aspecto de ruinas por meteorización y desmantelamiento.","en":"Relief with a ruin-like appearance due to weathering and dismantling."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-ruiniforme-caos-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"es":"cerro ruiniforme poligenetico","en":"ruiniform hill; block chaos"},"altLabel":{"es":["caos de bloques"]},"definition":{"es":"Relieve con aspecto de ruinas por meteorización y desmantelamiento.","en":"Relief with a ruin-like appearance due to weathering and dismantling."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cueva","prefLabel":{"es":"cueva","en":"cave"},"definition":{"es":"Cavidad subterránea natural de origen kárstico.","en":"A natural underground cavity of karst origin."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina","prefLabel":{"es":"dolina","en":"doline; sinkhole"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión cerrada de planta circular o elíptica formada por disolución kárstica.","en":"A closed depression of circular or elliptical plan formed by karst dissolution."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-capturada","prefLabel":{"es":"dolina capturada","en":"captured doline"},"definition":{"es":"Dolina conectada al drenaje superficial por captura.","en":"A doline connected to surface drainage by capture."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-con-borde-difuso","prefLabel":{"es":"dolina con borde difuso","en":"doline with diffuse rim"},"definition":{"es":"Dolina cuyo borde ha sido suavizado por erosión.","en":"A doline whose rim has been smoothed by erosion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-con-fondo-plano","prefLabel":{"es":"dolina con fondo plano","en":"flat-bottomed doline"},"definition":{"es":"Dolina con fondo horizontal ocupado generalmente por arcillas de descalcificación.","en":"A doline with a horizontal bottom generally occupied by decalcification clays."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-de-hundimiento-o-dolina-en-ventana","prefLabel":{"es":"dolina de hundimiento o dolina en ventana","en":"collapse doline; window doline"},"definition":{"es":"Dolina formada por colapso del techo de una cavidad subterránea.","en":"A doline formed by collapse of the roof of an underground cavity."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-de-karst-cubierto-dolina-aluvial","prefLabel":{"es":"dolina de karst cubierto; dolina aluvial","en":"covered karst doline; alluvial doline"},"definition":{"es":"Dolina formada en materiales que recubren el karst subyacente.","en":"A doline formed in materials covering the underlying karst."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-en-embudo","prefLabel":{"es":"dolina en embudo","en":"funnel-shaped doline"},"definition":{"es":"Dolina con forma de embudo y paredes inclinadas convergentes.","en":"A funnel-shaped doline with converging inclined walls."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/pequenya-dolina","prefLabel":{"es":"pequeña dolina","en":"small doline"},"definition":{"es":"Dolina de dimensiones reducidas.","en":"A doline of small dimensions."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-pequenyas-dolinas","prefLabel":{"es":"campo de pequeñas dolinas","en":"small doline field"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con alta densidad de dolinas de pequeño tamaño.","en":"An area with a high density of small dolines."}}]}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-y-dorso-de-ballena","prefLabel":{"es":"domo y dorso de ballena","en":"dome and whaleback"},"definition":{"es":"Forma redondeada en roca desnuda producida por meteorización.","en":"A rounded form in bare rock produced by weathering."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ferruginizaciones-rubefacciones","prefLabel":{"es":"ferruginizaciones; rubefacciones","en":"ferruginization; rubefaction"},"definition":{"es":"Enriquecimiento en óxidos de hierro que da coloración rojiza a la roca o suelo.","en":"Iron oxide enrichment giving a reddish coloration to rock or soil."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lapiaz","prefLabel":{"es":"lapiaz","en":"karren; lapiaz"},"definition":{"es":"Formas de disolución en la superficie de rocas calcáreas.","en":"Dissolution forms on the surface of calcareous rocks."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-lapiaces","prefLabel":{"es":"campo de lapiaces","en":"karren field"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con desarrollo extenso de lapiaces.","en":"An area with extensive karren development."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lapiaz-cubierto","prefLabel":{"es":"lapiaz cubierto","en":"covered karren"},"definition":{"es":"Lapiaz totalmente cubierto por suelo, visible solo en corte.","en":"Karren totally covered by soil, visible only in cross section."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lapiaz-semicubierto","prefLabel":{"es":"lapiaz semicubierto","en":"semi-covered karren"},"definition":{"es":"Lapiaz parcialmente cubierto por suelo o vegetación.","en":"Karren partially covered by soil or vegetation."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-alveolo-de-alteracion-nava","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de alveolo de alteración; nava","en":"weathering depression limit; nava"},"definition":{"es":"Límite de una depresión cerrada formada por meteorización química intensa.","en":"Limit of a closed depression formed by intense chemical weathering."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-area-con-intensa-karstificacion","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de área con intensa karstificación","en":"intensely karstified area limit"},"definition":{"es":"Límite de una zona con desarrollo kárstico muy avanzado.","en":"Limit of a zone with very advanced karst development."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-cuenca-endorreica-de-origen-karstico","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de cuenca endorreica de origen kárstico","en":"karst endorheic basin limit"},"definition":{"es":"Límite de una cuenca sin drenaje externo originada por procesos kársticos.","en":"Limit of a basin without external drainage originated by karst processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-paleopolje","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de paleopolje","en":"palaeo-polje limit"},"definition":{"es":"Límite de un antiguo polje ya no funcional.","en":"Limit of a former polje no longer functional."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-polje-funcional","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de polje funcional","en":"functional polje limit"},"definition":{"es":"Límite de un polje actualmente funcional con drenaje kárstico.","en":"Limit of a currently functional polje with karst drainage."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/meteorizacion-en-general","prefLabel":{"es":"meteorización en general","en":"weathering (general)"},"definition":{"es":"Procesos de alteración de la roca por agentes atmosféricos y químicos.","en":"Rock alteration processes by atmospheric and chemical agents."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/microformas-de-alteracion","prefLabel":{"es":"microformas de alteración","en":"weathering microforms"},"definition":{"es":"Formas de pequeña escala producidas por meteorización en superficies rocosas.","en":"Small-scale forms produced by weathering on rock surfaces."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ponor","prefLabel":{"es":"ponor","en":"ponor"},"definition":{"es":"Abertura en la roca por donde el agua de un polje o depresión kárstica drena al subsuelo.","en":"An opening in rock through which water from a polje or karst depression drains underground."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/puente-o-tunel-natural","prefLabel":{"es":"puente o túnel natural","en":"natural bridge or tunnel"},"definition":{"es":"Arco o túnel natural en roca formado por disolución kárstica o erosión.","en":"A natural arch or tunnel in rock formed by karst dissolution or erosion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-karstico-hum","prefLabel":{"es":"relieve kárstico; hum","en":"karst relief; hum"},"definition":{"es":"Relieve residual positivo en un paisaje kárstico.","en":"Positive residual relief in a karst landscape."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/roca-aislada-pinaculo-rocoso-tor","prefLabel":{"es":"roca aislada; pináculo rocoso; tor","en":"tor; isolated rock pillar"},"definition":{"es":"Relieve residual aislado formado por meteorización diferencial.","en":"An isolated residual relief formed by differential weathering."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/sales","prefLabel":{"es":"sales","en":"salt deposits"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulaciones de sales en superficie por evaporación.","en":"Surface salt accumulations by evaporation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/silicificaciones","prefLabel":{"es":"silicificaciones","en":"silicification"},"definition":{"es":"Reemplazamiento por sílice de los minerales originales de la roca.","en":"Replacement of original rock minerals by silica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/sima","prefLabel":{"es":"sima","en":"pothole; shaft"},"definition":{"es":"Cavidad vertical profunda en terreno kárstico.","en":"A deep vertical cavity in karst terrain."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/sumidero","prefLabel":{"es":"sumidero","en":"swallow hole; sinkhole"},"definition":{"es":"Punto donde un curso de agua superficial desaparece en el subsuelo kárstico.","en":"Point where a surface watercourse disappears into the karst underground."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/surgencia","prefLabel":{"es":"surgencia","en":"karst spring; resurgence"},"definition":{"es":"Punto de salida de aguas subterráneas kársticas a la superficie.","en":"Emergence point of karst groundwater at the surface."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/tafoni","prefLabel":{"es":"tafoni","en":"tafoni"},"definition":{"es":"Cavidades de meteorización en superficies rocosas.","en":"Weathering cavities on rock surfaces."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/toba-travertino","prefLabel":{"es":"toba; travertino","en":"tufa; travertine"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito de carbonato cálcico precipitado por aguas ricas en CO2.","en":"Calcium carbonate deposit precipitated by CO2-rich waters."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/toba-masa-travertinica","prefLabel":{"es":"toba; masa travertínica","en":"tufa; travertine mass"},"definition":{"es":"Masa o edificio de travertino de dimensiones significativas.","en":"A travertine mass or edifice of significant dimensions."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/uvala","prefLabel":{"es":"uvala","en":"uvala"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión kárstica de mayor tamaño formada por coalescencia de varias dolinas.","en":"A larger karst depression formed by coalescence of several dolines."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/valle-ciego","prefLabel":{"es":"valle ciego","en":"blind valley"},"definition":{"es":"Valle fluvial que termina bruscamente en un sumidero kárstico.","en":"A fluvial valley that ends abruptly at a karst sinkhole."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-glaciales-fluvioglaciares-y-de-permafrost","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos glaciales, fluvioglaciares y de permafrost","en":"nival, periglacial and permafrost features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a entornos de clima frío, con nieve, pero no glaciales; paisajes geomorfológicos y formas de relieve próximos a glaciares y placas de hielo; paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a tierras, suelos o rocas que se mantienen a 0º C o menos durante dos años como mínimo.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to snow, non-glacial, cold climate environments; geomorphologic landscapes and landforms occurring in the vicinity of glaciers and ice sheets; geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to ground, soil, or rock that remains at or below 0º C for at least two years."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-glaciales-glaciofluviales-glaciolacustres-y-glaciomarinos","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos glaciales, glaciofluviales, glaciolacustres y glaciomarinos","en":"glacial, glaciofluvial, glaciolacustrine and glaciomarine features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a entornos glaciales, glaciofluviales, glaciolacustres y glaciomarinos.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to to glacial, glaciofluvial, glaciolacustrine and glaciomarine environments."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acumulacion-de-origen-glaciar-indiferenciada-till","prefLabel":{"es":"acumulación de origen glaciar indiferenciada; till","en":"undifferentiated glacial deposit; till"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito glaciar no clasificado en un tipo específico de morrena.","en":"Glacial deposit not classified into a specific moraine type."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/anillos-o-circulos-de-piedra","prefLabel":{"es":"anillos o círculos de piedra","en":"stone circles"},"definition":{"es":"Patrones circulares de piedras formados por procesos de hielo-deshielo.","en":"Circular stone patterns formed by freeze-thaw processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-con-cesped-almohadillado","prefLabel":{"es":"área con césped almohadillado","en":"tussock area"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con montículos de vegetación en cojín típicos de ambientes fríos.","en":"Area with cushion vegetation mounds typical of cold environments."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-con-suelos-poligonales","prefLabel":{"es":"área con suelos poligonales","en":"patterned ground area"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con patrones poligonales en el suelo formados por procesos periglaciales.","en":"Area with polygonal soil patterns formed by periglacial processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arista","prefLabel":{"es":"arista","en":"arête"},"definition":{"es":"Cresta estrecha y aguda entre dos circos o valles glaciares.","en":"A narrow and sharp ridge between two cirques or glacial valleys."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/bloques-erraticos","prefLabel":{"es":"bloques erráticos","en":"erratic boulders"},"definition":{"es":"Bloques rocosos transportados por un glaciar lejos de su lugar de origen.","en":"Rock boulders transported by a glacier far from their place of origin."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-terraza-sobre-depositos-fluvioglaciares","prefLabel":{"es":"borde de terraza sobre depósitos fluvioglaciares","en":"fluvioglacial terrace edge"},"definition":{"es":"Borde de una terraza constituida por depósitos fluvioglaciares.","en":"Edge of a terrace composed of fluvioglacial deposits."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cabecera-de-avalancha-o-alud","prefLabel":{"es":"cabecera de avalancha o alud","en":"avalanche starting zone"},"definition":{"es":"Zona de arranque de una avalancha de nieve.","en":"Starting zone of a snow avalanche."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cabecera-de-avalancha-o-alud-difuso-o-degradado","prefLabel":{"es":"cabecera de avalancha o alud difuso o degradado","en":"diffuse or degraded avalanche starting zone"},"definition":{"es":"Zona de arranque de avalancha con morfología suavizada.","en":"Avalanche starting zone with smoothed morphology."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cambio-de-pendiente-del-valle-glaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"cambio de pendiente del valle glaciar","en":"glacial valley slope change"},"definition":{"es":"Cambio de pendiente longitudinal en el perfil de un valle glaciar.","en":"Longitudinal slope change in the profile of a glacial valley."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-supraglaciar-proglaciar-o-subglaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"canal supraglaciar, proglaciar o subglaciar","en":"supraglacial, proglacial or subglacial channel"},"definition":{"es":"Canal de drenaje en la superficie, frente o base de un glaciar.","en":"Drainage channel on the surface, front or base of a glacier."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canchal-pedriza-pedrera","prefLabel":{"es":"canchal; pedriza; pedrera","en":"scree; talus"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulación de fragmentos rocosos angulosos al pie de una pared o escarpe.","en":"Accumulation of angular rock fragments at the foot of a wall or scarp."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cavidades","prefLabel":{"es":"cavidades","en":"cavities"},"definition":{"es":"Oquedades formadas en la masa de hielo o en su contacto con la roca.","en":"Hollows formed in the ice mass or at its contact with rock."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/charca-laguna","prefLabel":{"es":"charca; laguna","en":"pond; small lake"},"definition":{"es":"Pequeña masa de agua estancada de origen glaciar.","en":"A small body of standing water of glacial origin."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/circo-glaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"circo glaciar","en":"glacial cirque"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión semicircular en forma de anfiteatro excavada por un glaciar en la cabecera de un valle.","en":"A semicircular amphitheatre-shaped depression excavated by a glacier at the head of a valley."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/circo-glaciar-degradado","prefLabel":{"es":"circo glaciar degradado","en":"degraded glacial cirque"},"definition":{"es":"Circo glaciar cuya morfología ha sido suavizada por procesos erosivos posteriores.","en":"A glacial cirque whose morphology has been smoothed by subsequent erosional processes."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado-de-difluencia-glaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"collado de difluencia glaciar","en":"glacial diffluence col"},"definition":{"es":"Paso entre dos valles por donde un glaciar desborda hacia un valle adyacente.","en":"A pass between two valleys where a glacier overflows into an adjacent valley."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado-de-transfluencia-glaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"collado de transfluencia glaciar","en":"glacial transfluence col"},"definition":{"es":"Paso por donde el hielo de un glaciar principal fluye hacia un valle adyacente.","en":"A pass where ice from a main glacier flows into an adjacent valley."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-avalancha-o-alud","prefLabel":{"es":"cono de avalancha o alud","en":"avalanche cone"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito en forma de cono en la base de un corredor de avalancha.","en":"Cone-shaped deposit at the base of an avalanche track."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-hielo","prefLabel":{"es":"cono de hielo","en":"ice cone"},"definition":{"es":"Estructura cónica formada por acumulación y congelación de agua.","en":"A conical structure formed by water accumulation and freezing."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-proglaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"cono proglaciar","en":"proglacial cone"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito en forma de cono formado por aguas de fusión glaciar.","en":"A cone-shaped deposit formed by glacial meltwater."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordal-o-divisoria-montanyosa","prefLabel":{"es":"cordal o divisoria montañosa","en":"mountain ridge"},"definition":{"es":"Cresta montañosa que constituye una divisoria de aguas.","en":"A mountain crest that constitutes a watershed divide."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordones-contornos-o-crestas-morrenicas","prefLabel":{"es":"cordones, contornos o crestas morrénicas","en":"morainic ridges"},"definition":{"es":"Crestas alargadas formadas por acumulación morrénica.","en":"Elongated ridges formed by morainic accumulation."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordones-contornos-o-crestas-morrenicas-difusos-o-degradados","prefLabel":{"es":"cordones, contornos o crestas morrénicas difusos o degradados","en":"diffuse or degraded morainic ridges"},"definition":{"es":"Crestas morrénicas suavizadas por erosión posterior.","en":"Morainic ridges smoothed by subsequent erosion."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordones-o-contornos-morrenicos-de-nevero","prefLabel":{"es":"cordones o contornos morrénicos de nevero","en":"snow patch morainic ridges"},"definition":{"es":"Crestas morrénicas formadas al pie de un nevero.","en":"Morainic ridges formed at the base of a snow patch."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/corredor-de-avalancha-o-alud","prefLabel":{"es":"corredor de avalancha o alud","en":"avalanche track"},"definition":{"es":"Canal o corredor por donde desciende una avalancha de nieve.","en":"Channel or track along which a snow avalanche descends."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/corredor-rocoso-campo-de-rocas-rio-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"es":"corredor rocoso; campo de rocas; río de bloques","en":"blockstream; block field"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulación alargada de bloques rocosos que desciende una ladera por procesos periglaciales.","en":"Elongated accumulation of rock blocks descending a slope by periglacial processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cresta-morrenica-con-indicacion-de-flujo-de-hielo","prefLabel":{"es":"cresta morrénica con indicación de flujo de hielo","en":"morainic ridge with ice flow indication"},"definition":{"es":"Cresta morrénica con indicación de la dirección del flujo glaciar.","en":"Morainic ridge with indication of glacial flow direction."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cubeta-de-sobreexcavacion","prefLabel":{"es":"cubeta de sobreexcavación","en":"overdeepened basin"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión excavada por el glaciar por debajo del perfil de equilibrio del valle.","en":"A depression excavated by the glacier below the valley equilibrium profile."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deposito-de-opturacion-kame","prefLabel":{"es":"depósito de opturación; kame","en":"kame deposit"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito de materiales fluvioglaciares acumulados en contacto con el hielo.","en":"Fluvioglacial deposit accumulated in contact with ice."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrubios-ordenados-o-estratificados-grèzes-litees","prefLabel":{"es":"derrubios ordenados o estratificados; grèzes litées","en":"stratified slope deposits; grèzes litées"},"definition":{"es":"Depósitos de ladera con alternancia de capas de diferente granulometría de origen periglaciar.","en":"Slope deposits with alternating layers of different grain size of periglacial origin."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/direccion-de-flujo-del-hielo","prefLabel":{"es":"dirección de flujo del hielo","en":"ice flow direction"},"definition":{"es":"Indicación de la dirección de movimiento de un glaciar.","en":"Indication of the direction of glacier movement."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/drumlin","prefLabel":{"es":"drumlin","en":"drumlin"},"definition":{"es":"Colina alargada de materiales glaciares con forma de cuchara invertida, orientada en la dirección del flujo del hielo.","en":"An elongated hill of glacial materials shaped like an inverted spoon, oriented in the ice flow direction."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/estrias","prefLabel":{"es":"estrías","en":"striations"},"definition":{"es":"Marcas lineales finas sobre la roca producidas por abrasión glaciar.","en":"Fine linear marks on rock produced by glacial abrasion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/garganta-subglaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"garganta subglaciar","en":"subglacial gorge"},"definition":{"es":"Garganta excavada por aguas de fusión bajo un glaciar.","en":"A gorge excavated by meltwater beneath a glacier."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/gelifluxion","prefLabel":{"es":"gelifluxión","en":"gelifluction"},"definition":{"es":"Flujo lento del suelo saturado sobre un substrato helado.","en":"Slow flow of saturated soil over a frozen substrate."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glaciar-de-rocas","prefLabel":{"es":"glaciar de rocas","en":"rock glacier"},"definition":{"es":"Masa de derrubios con hielo intersticial que se mueve lentamente ladera abajo.","en":"A debris mass with interstitial ice that moves slowly downslope."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glaciar-y-helero","prefLabel":{"es":"glaciar y helero","en":"glacier and permanent snow field"},"definition":{"es":"Masa de hielo que se mueve lentamente ladera abajo o campo de nieve permanente.","en":"A mass of ice moving slowly downslope or a permanent snow field."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/guirnaldas-de-piedras","prefLabel":{"es":"guirnaldas de piedras","en":"stone garlands"},"definition":{"es":"Alineaciones curvas de piedras en laderas producidas por procesos periglaciales.","en":"Curved stone alignments on slopes produced by periglacial processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hidrolacolito","prefLabel":{"es":"hidrolacolito","en":"hydrolaccolith"},"definition":{"es":"Montículo formado por congelación de agua en el subsuelo que levanta la superficie.","en":"A mound formed by freezing of subsurface water that uplifts the surface."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ladera-con-reptacion-creep","prefLabel":{"es":"ladera con reptación; creep","en":"slope with creep"},"definition":{"es":"Vertiente afectada por movimiento lento y continuo del suelo por ciclos de hielo-deshielo.","en":"A slope affected by slow continuous soil movement due to freeze-thaw cycles."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lago-de-montanya-ibon","prefLabel":{"es":"lago de montaña; ibón","en":"mountain lake; tarn"},"definition":{"es":"Lago de montaña de origen glaciar situado generalmente en un circo.","en":"A mountain lake of glacial origin generally located in a cirque."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lago-o-cubeta-colmatada","prefLabel":{"es":"lago o cubeta colmatada","en":"infilled lake or basin"},"definition":{"es":"Lago glaciar o cubeta que ha sido rellenada por sedimentos.","en":"A glacial lake or basin that has been filled by sediments."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lapiaz-en-hielo","prefLabel":{"es":"lapiaz en hielo","en":"ice karren"},"definition":{"es":"Formas de disolución o fusión en la superficie del hielo similares al lapiaz en roca.","en":"Dissolution or melting forms on ice surface similar to rock karren."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-valle-en-artesa","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de valle en artesa","en":"U-shaped valley limit"},"definition":{"es":"Límite topográfico de un valle glaciar con perfil transversal en U.","en":"Topographic limit of a glacial valley with a U-shaped cross section."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-valle-en-artesa-degradado","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de valle en artesa degradado","en":"degraded U-shaped valley limit"},"definition":{"es":"Límite de un valle glaciar en artesa suavizado por erosión posterior.","en":"Limit of a U-shaped glacial valley smoothed by subsequent erosion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-zona-glaciada","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de zona glaciada","en":"glaciated area limit"},"definition":{"es":"Límite del área que fue cubierta por hielo glaciar.","en":"Limit of the area that was covered by glacial ice."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lobulo-de-gelifluxion","prefLabel":{"es":"lóbulo de gelifluxión","en":"gelifluction lobe"},"definition":{"es":"Forma lobulada producida por gelifluxión en una ladera.","en":"A lobe-shaped form produced by gelifluction on a slope."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lugar-con-rocas-aborregadas","prefLabel":{"es":"lugar con rocas aborregadas","en":"roches moutonnées area"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con afloramientos rocosos esculpidos por abrasión glaciar con forma asimétrica.","en":"Area with rock outcrops sculpted by glacial abrasion with asymmetric shape."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/manto-proglaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"manto proglaciar","en":"proglacial outwash plain"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito extenso y plano formado por aguas de fusión glaciar.","en":"An extensive flat deposit formed by glacial meltwater."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena","prefLabel":{"es":"morrena","en":"moraine"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulación de materiales transportados y depositados por un glaciar.","en":"Accumulation of materials transported and deposited by a glacier."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena-de-fondo","prefLabel":{"es":"morrena de fondo","en":"ground moraine"},"definition":{"es":"Morrena depositada bajo el glaciar en forma de manto.","en":"Moraine deposited beneath the glacier as a mantle."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena-frontal","prefLabel":{"es":"morrena frontal","en":"terminal moraine"},"definition":{"es":"Morrena depositada en el frente de un glaciar.","en":"Moraine deposited at the front of a glacier."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena-lateral-o-central","prefLabel":{"es":"morrena lateral o central","en":"lateral or medial moraine"},"definition":{"es":"Morrena depositada en los flancos o en el centro de un glaciar.","en":"Moraine deposited on the flanks or centre of a glacier."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena-de-nevero","prefLabel":{"es":"morrena de nevero","en":"snow patch moraine"},"definition":{"es":"Morrena asociada a un nevero permanente o semipermanente.","en":"Moraine associated with a permanent or semi-permanent snow patch."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/nicho-o-circo-de-nivacion","prefLabel":{"es":"nicho o circo de nivación","en":"nivation hollow"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión poco profunda formada por procesos de nivación al pie de un nevero.","en":"A shallow depression formed by nivation processes at the base of a snow patch."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/nicho-o-circo-de-nivacion-difuso-o-degradado","prefLabel":{"es":"nicho o circo de nivación difuso o degradado","en":"diffuse or degraded nivation hollow"},"definition":{"es":"Nicho de nivación cuya forma ha sido suavizada por erosión posterior.","en":"A nivation hollow whose shape has been smoothed by subsequent erosion."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/nieve-perpetua","prefLabel":{"es":"nieve perpetua","en":"permanent snow"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulación de nieve que persiste durante todo el año.","en":"Snow accumulation that persists throughout the year."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/pico-principal-aguja-hörn","prefLabel":{"es":"pico principal, aguja; hörn","en":"main peak; horn"},"definition":{"es":"Cima piramidal aguda esculpida por erosión glaciar.","en":"A sharp pyramidal peak sculpted by glacial erosion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/roca-aborregada","prefLabel":{"es":"roca aborregada","en":"roche moutonnée"},"definition":{"es":"Afloramiento rocoso esculpido por abrasión glaciar, pulido en la cara de avance y arrancado en la cara opuesta.","en":"Rock outcrop sculpted by glacial abrasion, polished on the advancing face and plucked on the opposite face."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/sendas-de-ganado-terracillas-pies-de-vaca","prefLabel":{"es":"sendas de ganado; terracillas; pies de vaca","en":"cattle tracks; terracettes"},"definition":{"es":"Pequeños escalones en laderas producidos por pisoteo de ganado o reptación.","en":"Small steps on slopes produced by cattle trampling or creep."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/seracs-rimayas","prefLabel":{"es":"seracs; rimayas","en":"seracs; bergschrund"},"definition":{"es":"Bloques de hielo separados por grietas en zonas de fuerte pendiente del glaciar; grieta en la cabecera.","en":"Ice blocks separated by crevasses in steep glacier zones; headwall crevasse."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/simas","prefLabel":{"es":"simas","en":"crevasses"},"definition":{"es":"Grietas profundas en la masa de hielo de un glaciar.","en":"Deep cracks in the ice mass of a glacier."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/suelos-estriados","prefLabel":{"es":"suelos estriados","en":"striped ground"},"definition":{"es":"Patrón de bandas alternas de material grueso y fino en una ladera por procesos de hielo-deshielo.","en":"Pattern of alternating bands of coarse and fine material on a slope due to freeze-thaw processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-abrasion","prefLabel":{"es":"superficie de abrasión","en":"abrasion surface"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie rocosa pulida y estriada por abrasión glaciar.","en":"Rock surface polished and striated by glacial abrasion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-o-rellano-de-crioplanacion","prefLabel":{"es":"superficie o rellano de crioplanación","en":"cryoplanation surface"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie plana formada por procesos de crioplanación en ambiente periglaciar.","en":"Flat surface formed by cryoplanation processes in a periglacial environment."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/talud-o-cono-de-derrubios","prefLabel":{"es":"talud o cono de derrubios","en":"talus or debris cone"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulación de derrubios al pie de una pared rocosa formando un cono o talud.","en":"Debris accumulation at the foot of a rock wall forming a cone or talus."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-proglaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza proglaciar","en":"proglacial terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Terraza formada por depósitos fluvioglaciares.","en":"A terrace formed by fluvioglacial deposits."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera","prefLabel":{"es":"turbera","en":"peat bog"},"definition":{"es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba).","en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera-en-ambiente-glaciar-y-periglaciar","prefLabel":{"es":"turbera en ambiente lacustra glaciar y periglaciar","en":"peat bog"},"definition":{"es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba).","en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/umbral-difuso","prefLabel":{"es":"umbral difuso","en":"diffuse threshold"},"definition":{"es":"Resalte rocoso poco marcado en el lecho de un valle glaciar.","en":"A poorly defined rocky step in the floor of a glacial valley."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/umbral-neto","prefLabel":{"es":"umbral neto","en":"distinct threshold"},"definition":{"es":"Resalte rocoso bien definido en el lecho de un valle glaciar.","en":"A well-defined rocky step in the floor of a glacial valley."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"es":"vertiente de bloques","en":"block slope"},"definition":{"es":"Vertiente cubierta por bloques rocosos producidos por gelifracción.","en":"A slope covered by rock blocks produced by frost shattering."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/zona-o-superficie-de-pulido-y-abrasion-con-indicacion-de-flujo","prefLabel":{"es":"zona o superficie de pulido y abrasión con indicación de flujo","en":"polished and abraded surface with flow indication"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie glacialmente pulida con estrías que indican la dirección del flujo del hielo.","en":"Glacially polished surface with striations indicating ice flow direction."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-hidrotermales","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos hidrotermales","en":"hydrothermal features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados con procesos hidrotermales.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to hydrothermal processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-lacustres","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos lacustres","en":"lacustrine features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados con masas de agua interiores permanentes (lagos).","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to inland permanent water bodies (lakes)."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-endorreica-con-salinizacion-superficial-playa-salina","prefLabel":{"es":"área endorreica con salinización superficial; playa salina","en":"salt flat; saline playa"},"definition":{"es":"Área endorréica con precipitación de sales en superficie.","en":"An endorheic area with surface salt precipitation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-endorreica-playa-encharcamiento-temporal","prefLabel":{"es":"área endorréica; playa; encharcamiento temporal","en":"endorheic area; playa"},"definition":{"es":"Zona sin drenaje externo donde el agua se acumula temporalmente.","en":"An area without external drainage where water accumulates temporarily."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-pantanosa","prefLabel":{"es":"área pantanosa","en":"marshy area"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con suelo permanentemente saturado de agua.","en":"An area with permanently waterlogged soil."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/charca-labajo-bodon-estacional","prefLabel":{"es":"charca; labajo; bodón estacional","en":"seasonal pond"},"definition":{"es":"Pequeña masa de agua estancada de carácter estacional.","en":"A small seasonal body of standing water."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/charca-labajo-bodon-permanente","prefLabel":{"es":"charca; labajo; bodón permanente","en":"permanent pond"},"definition":{"es":"Pequeña masa de agua estancada de carácter permanente.","en":"A small permanent body of standing water."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe","en":"scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Talud abrupto de origen poligénico.","en":"An abrupt slope of polygenetic origin."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-fosil","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe fosil","en":"fossil scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe lacustre que ya no está en contacto con una masa de agua.","en":"A lacustrine scarp no longer in contact with a water body."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpeescarpe-en-ambiente-lacustre","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe en ambiente lacustre","en":"scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Talud abrupto de origen poligénico.","en":"An abrupt slope of polygenetic origin."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/laguna","prefLabel":{"es":"laguna","en":"lagoon; small lake"},"definition":{"es":"Masa de agua de pequeña extensión y poca profundidad.","en":"A water body of small extent and shallow depth."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/laguna-colmatada-o-desecada","prefLabel":{"es":"laguna colmatada o desecada","en":"infilled or desiccated lagoon"},"definition":{"es":"Laguna rellenada por sedimentos o desecada.","en":"A lagoon filled with sediments or desiccated."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/laguna-estacional","prefLabel":{"es":"laguna estacional","en":"seasonal lagoon"},"definition":{"es":"Laguna que se seca en determinadas épocas del año.","en":"A lagoon that dries up during certain times of the year."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/laguna-permanente","prefLabel":{"es":"laguna permanente","en":"permanent lagoon"},"definition":{"es":"Laguna con agua durante todo el año.","en":"A lagoon with water throughout the year."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-cuenca-endorreica","prefLabel":{"es":"límite de cuenca endorréica","en":"endorheic basin limit"},"definition":{"es":"Divisoria que delimita una cuenca sin drenaje al mar.","en":"Divide delimiting a basin without drainage to the sea."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ojos-de-agua","prefLabel":{"es":"ojos de agua","en":"water eyes; springs"},"definition":{"es":"Surgencias puntuales de agua subterránea.","en":"Point emergences of groundwater."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/reborde-de-terraza-con-indicacion-de-cota-en-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"reborde de terraza con indicación de cota en metros","en":"terrace edge with elevation in metres"},"definition":{"es":"Borde de una terraza lacustre con indicación de su cota.","en":"Edge of a lacustrine terrace with elevation indication."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-lacustre","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza lacustre","en":"lacustrine terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie plana elevada que representa un antiguo nivel de un lago.","en":"An elevated flat surface representing a former lake level."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera","prefLabel":{"es":"turbera","en":"peat bog"},"definition":{"es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba).","en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera-en-ambiente-lacustre","prefLabel":{"es":"turbera en ambiente lacustre","en":"peat bog"},"definition":{"es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba).","en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat)."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-marinos-litorales-y-de-humedales-costeros","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos marinos, litorales y de humedales costeros","en":"marine, littoral and coastal wetlands features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a la dinámica del oleaje y de las mareas desarrollada en entornos marinos, de aguas poco profundas, cercanos a la costa y litorales, y relativos a humedales con vegetación y poco profundos.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to wave or tidal dynamics developed in marine, shallow marine, near-shore and littoral zone environments, and those related to vegetated and / or shallow wet areas"},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/abanico-de-arena-washover-fan","prefLabel":{"es":"abanico de arena; washover fan","en":"washover fan"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito en abanico de arena transportada por olas de tormenta sobre un cordón litoral.","en":"Fan-shaped sand deposit transported by storm waves over a beach ridge."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado","prefLabel":{"es":"acantilado","en":"cliff"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe vertical o subvertical costero tallado por erosión marina.","en":"A vertical or subvertical coastal scarp carved by marine erosion."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado-entre-25-y-100-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"acantilado entre 25 y 100 metros","en":"cliff 25-100 m"},"definition":{"es":"Acantilado costero de entre 25 y 100 metros de altura.","en":"A coastal cliff between 25 and 100 metres high."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado-fosil","prefLabel":{"es":"acantilado fósil","en":"fossil cliff"},"definition":{"es":"Acantilado relicto separado de la línea de costa actual.","en":"A relict cliff separated from the current coastline."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado-inferior-a-25-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"acantilado inferior a 25 metros","en":"cliff less than 25 m"},"definition":{"es":"Acantilado costero de menos de 25 metros de altura.","en":"A coastal cliff less than 25 metres high."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado-superior-a-100-metros","prefLabel":{"es":