owth phases of a beach ridge."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza","en":"terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie plana elevada respecto al cauce actual, que representa un antiguo nivel del río.","en":"A flat surface elevated above the current channel, representing a former river level."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-erosiva","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza erosiva","en":"erosional terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Terraza tallada en la roca sin depósito aluvial significativo.","en":"A terrace carved into rock without significant alluvial deposit."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-no-ciclica-de-encajamiento-convergente","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza no cíclica (de encajamiento; convergente)","en":"non-cyclic terrace (entrenching; convergent)"},"definition":{"es":"Terraza formada por encajamiento progresivo sin relación con ciclos climáticos.","en":"Terrace formed by progressive entrenchment without relation to climatic cycles."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-travertinica","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza travertínica","en":"travertine terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Terraza formada por precipitación de carbonato cálcico (travertino).","en":"Terrace formed by calcium carbonate (travertine) precipitation."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-litoral","prefLabel":{"es":"terraza litoral","en":"terrace"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie plana elevada respecto al cauce actual, que representa un antiguo nivel del río.","en":"A flat surface elevated above the current channel, representing a former river level."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera","prefLabel":{"es":"turbera","en":"peat bog"},"definition":{"es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba).","en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/zona-de-rompiente-zona-intermareal","prefLabel":{"es":"zona de rompiente; zona intermareal","en":"surf zone; intertidal zone"},"definition":{"es":"Franja litoral entre los niveles de marea alta y baja.","en":"Coastal strip between high and low tide levels."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-relacionados-con-las-laderas-y-con-la-gravedad","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos relacionados con las laderas y con la gravedad","en":"slope and gravitational features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados con entornos de ladera; paisajes geomorfológicos y formas de relieve desarrollados por efecto de la acción de la gravedad.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to slope environments; geomorphologic landscapes and landforms developed under the action of the gravitational force."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acarcavamiento-embrionario","prefLabel":{"es":"acarcavamiento embrionario","en":"incipient gullying"},"definition":{"es":"Fase inicial de formación de cárcavas en una vertiente.","en":"Initial phase of gully formation on a slope."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/caidas-de-bloques-desprendimientos-derrumbes","prefLabel":{"es":"caídas de bloques; desprendimientos; derrumbes","en":"rockfall; rock collapse"},"definition":{"es":"Desprendimiento de bloques rocosos de un escarpe o pared.","en":"Detachment of rock blocks from a scarp or wall."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cambio-brusco-de-pendiente","prefLabel":{"es":"cambio brusco de pendiente","en":"abrupt slope break"},"definition":{"es":"Cambio repentino del ángulo de la pendiente en una vertiente.","en":"A sudden change in slope angle on a hillside."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canchal-pedriza","prefLabel":{"es":"canchal; pedriza","en":"scree; block field"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulación de fragmentos rocosos angulosos en una ladera.","en":"Accumulation of angular rock fragments on a slope."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cicatriz-de-despegue-producida-por-movimientos-en-masa","prefLabel":{"es":"cicatriz de despegue producida por movimientos en masa","en":"mass movement detachment scar"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie de rotura visible en la zona de arranque de un movimiento en masa.","en":"Visible rupture surface at the head zone of a mass movement."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/coluvion","prefLabel":{"es":"coluvión","en":"colluvium"},"definition":{"es":"Depósito de materiales sueltos acumulados al pie de una ladera por gravedad.","en":"A deposit of loose materials accumulated at the foot of a slope by gravity."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-o-talud-de-derrubios","prefLabel":{"es":"cono o talud de derrubios","en":"talus cone; scree slope"},"definition":{"es":"Acumulación de fragmentos rocosos al pie de una pared o escarpe formando un cono o talud.","en":"Accumulation of rock fragments at the foot of a wall or scarp forming a cone or talus."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrubios-ordenados","prefLabel":{"es":"derrubios ordenados","en":"stratified slope deposits"},"definition":{"es":"Depósitos de ladera con cierta ordenación o estratificación.","en":"Slope deposits with some ordering or stratification."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrumbe-avalancha","prefLabel":{"es":"derrumbe; avalancha","en":"rock avalanche"},"definition":{"es":"Movimiento rápido y masivo de rocas y derrubios ladera abajo.","en":"Rapid and massive downslope movement of rocks and debris."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deslizamiento","prefLabel":{"es":"deslizamiento","en":"landslide"},"definition":{"es":"Movimiento en masa de materiales ladera abajo a lo largo de una superficie de rotura.","en":"Downslope mass movement of materials along a failure surface."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deslizamiento-cartografiable","prefLabel":{"es":"deslizamiento cartografiable","en":"mappable landslide"},"definition":{"es":"Deslizamiento de dimensiones suficientes para ser representado en un mapa.","en":"A landslide of sufficient dimensions to be represented on a map."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/facetas-triangulares-de-vertiente","prefLabel":{"es":"facetas triangulares de vertiente","en":"triangular slope facets"},"definition":{"es":"Superficies triangulares en vertientes producidas por la intersección de valles transversales.","en":"Triangular surfaces on slopes produced by the intersection of transverse valleys."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/flujo","prefLabel":{"es":"flujo","en":"flow"},"definition":{"es":"Movimiento en masa con comportamiento de fluido viscoso.","en":"A mass movement with viscous fluid behavior."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ladera-con-reptacion","prefLabel":{"es":"ladera con reptación","en":"slope with creep"},"definition":{"es":"Vertiente afectada por movimiento lento y continuo del suelo o regolito.","en":"A slope affected by slow and continuous movement of soil or regolith."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lajamiento-sheeting","prefLabel":{"es":"lajamiento; sheeting","en":"sheeting"},"definition":{"es":"Fracturación de la roca en láminas paralelas a la superficie topográfica.","en":"Rock fracturing into sheets parallel to the topographic surface."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lobulo-o-colada-de-solifluxion","prefLabel":{"es":"lóbulo o colada de solifluxión","en":"solifluction lobe"},"definition":{"es":"Forma lobulada producida por solifluxión en una ladera.","en":"A lobe-shaped form produced by solifluction on a slope."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terracillas","prefLabel":{"es":"terracillas","en":"terracettes"},"definition":{"es":"Pequeños escalones paralelos a las curvas de nivel en una ladera, producidos por reptación o pisoteo.","en":"Small steps parallel to contour lines on a slope, produced by creep or trampling."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-con-bloques","prefLabel":{"es":"vertiente con bloques","en":"block-covered slope"},"definition":{"es":"Vertiente cubierta por bloques rocosos procedentes de la parte superior.","en":"A slope covered by rock blocks from the upper part."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-con-surcos-de-erosion-rills","prefLabel":{"es":"vertiente con surcos de erosión (rills)","en":"slope with rills"},"definition":{"es":"Vertiente con pequeños surcos lineales formados por escorrentía superficial.","en":"A slope with small linear grooves formed by surface runoff."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-regularizada","prefLabel":{"es":"vertiente regularizada","en":"regularized slope"},"definition":{"es":"Vertiente cuyo perfil ha sido suavizado por procesos de erosión y sedimentación.","en":"A slope whose profile has been smoothed by erosion and sedimentation processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-regularizada-y-disectada","prefLabel":{"es":"vertiente regularizada y disectada","en":"regularized and dissected slope"},"definition":{"es":"Vertiente regularizada que ha sido posteriormente incidida por cauces.","en":"A regularized slope that has been subsequently incised by channels."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/zona-con-solifluxion","prefLabel":{"es":"zona con solifluxión","en":"solifluction zone"},"definition":{"es":"Área afectada por flujo lento del suelo saturado sobre un substrato helado o impermeable.","en":"Area affected by slow flow of saturated soil over a frozen or impermeable substrate."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-tectonicos-y-estructurales","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos tectónicos y estructurales","en":"tectonic and structural features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve resultantes de estructuras regionales o locales de roca o de movimientos tectónicos o corticales; asimismo, paisajes geomorfológicos y formas de relieve de origen tectónico o exhumados predominantemente por la erosión del agua, con exclusión de las corrientes canalizadas perennes (es decir, fluviales o glaciofluviales), o por la erosión eólica.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to regional or local bedrock structures, or crustal movement; and geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related dominantly to water erosion but excluding perennial, channel flow (i.e. fluvial, glaciofluvial), or eolian erosion."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/alineacion-morfologica-con-control-estructural","prefLabel":{"es":"alineación morfológica con control estructural","en":"structurally controlled morphological alignment"},"definition":{"es":"Alineación de formas del relieve controlada por la estructura geológica subyacente.","en":"Alignment of relief forms controlled by the underlying geological structure."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/basculamiento","prefLabel":{"es":"basculamiento","en":"tilting"},"definition":{"es":"Inclinación de un bloque o superficie por movimientos tectónicos.","en":"Inclination of a block or surface due to tectonic movements."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico","prefLabel":{"es":"cerro cónico","en":"conical hill"},"definition":{"es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica.","en":"A conical terrain elevation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cresta-barra","prefLabel":{"es":"cresta; barra","en":"ridge; bar"},"definition":{"es":"Relieve positivo alargado y estrecho controlado por capas resistentes.","en":"Elongated and narrow positive relief controlled by resistant layers."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-contacto-diapirico","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe de contacto diapírico","en":"diapiric contact scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe topográfico originado en el contacto de un cuerpo diapírico con las rocas adyacentes.","en":"A topographic scarp formed at the contact of a diapiric body with adjacent rocks."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-contacto-intrusivo","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe de contacto intrusivo","en":"intrusive contact scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe topográfico originado en el contacto entre una roca intrusiva y la roca encajante.","en":"A topographic scarp formed at the contact between an intrusive rock and the host rock."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe de línea de falla","en":"fault-line scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe topográfico coincidente con el trazado de una falla.","en":"A topographic scarp coinciding with the trace of a fault."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-degradado","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe de línea de falla degradado","en":"degraded fault-line scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de falla cuya morfología ha sido suavizada por procesos erosivos.","en":"A fault-line scarp whose morphology has been smoothed by erosional processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-en-retroceso","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe de línea de falla en retroceso","en":"retreating fault-line scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de falla cuya posición se desplaza progresivamente por retroceso erosivo.","en":"A fault-line scarp whose position progressively shifts due to erosional retreat."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-exhumado","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe de línea de falla exhumado","en":"exhumed fault-line scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de falla que ha sido re-expuesto tras haber estado cubierto por materiales más recientes.","en":"A fault-line scarp re-exposed after having been covered by younger materials."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-inversa-o-cabalgamiento","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe de línea de falla inversa o cabalgamiento","en":"reverse or thrust fault-line scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe topográfico asociado a una falla inversa o cabalgamiento.","en":"A topographic scarp associated with a reverse or thrust fault."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-originado-por-erosion-diferencial","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe de línea de falla originado por erosión diferencial","en":"differential erosion fault-line scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe resultante de la erosión diferencial a lo largo de una línea de falla.","en":"A scarp resulting from differential erosion along a fault line."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe estructural","en":"structural scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe topográfico controlado por la disposición de las capas geológicas.","en":"A topographic scarp controlled by the arrangement of geological layers."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-horizontales-entre-25-100-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe estructural en capas horizontales (entre 25-100 metros)","en":"structural scarp in horizontal layers (25-100 m)"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de 25 a 100 m de altura en capas horizontales.","en":"A scarp 25 to 100 m high in horizontal layers."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-horizontales-inferior-a-25-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe estructural en capas horizontales (inferior a 25 metros)","en":"structural scarp in horizontal layers (<25 m)"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de menos de 25 m de altura en capas horizontales.","en":"A scarp less than 25 m high in horizontal layers."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-horizontales-superior-a-100-metros","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe estructural en capas horizontales (superior a 100 metros)","en":"structural scarp in horizontal layers (>100 m)"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de más de 100 m de altura en capas horizontales.","en":"A scarp over 100 m high in horizontal layers."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-monoclinales-entre-25-100-metros-cuesta","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe estructural en capas monoclinales (entre 25-100 metros); cuesta","en":"cuesta scarp (25-100 m)"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de 25 a 100 m en capas monoclinales formando una cuesta.","en":"A scarp 25 to 100 m in monoclinal layers forming a cuesta."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-monoclinales-inferior-a-25-metros-cuesta","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe estructural en capas monoclinales (inferior a 25 metros); cuesta","en":"cuesta scarp (<25 m)"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de menos de 25 m en capas monoclinales formando una cuesta.","en":"A scarp less than 25 m in monoclinal layers forming a cuesta."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-monoclinales-superior-a-100-metros-cuesta","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe estructural en capas monoclinales (superior a 100 metros); cuesta","en":"cuesta scarp (>100 m)"},"definition":{"es":"Escarpe de más de 100 m en capas monoclinales formando una cuesta.","en":"A scarp over 100 m in monoclinal layers forming a cuesta."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/facetas-triangulares-de-escarpe-de-falla","prefLabel":{"es":"facetas triangulares de escarpe de falla","en":"triangular facets of fault scarp"},"definition":{"es":"Superficies triangulares en la ladera de un escarpe de falla producidas por la intersección de valles transversales.","en":"Triangular surfaces on the slope of a fault scarp produced by the intersection of transverse valleys."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla","prefLabel":{"es":"falla","en":"fault"},"definition":{"es":"Fractura o zona de fractura a lo largo de la cual ha habido desplazamiento de los bloques contiguos.","en":"A fracture or zone of fractures along which there has been displacement of the adjacent blocks."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla-en-direccion-desgarre","prefLabel":{"es":"falla en dirección; desgarre","en":"strike-slip fault"},"definition":{"es":"Falla en la que el desplazamiento es predominantemente horizontal y paralelo al rumbo de la falla.","en":"A fault in which the displacement is predominantly horizontal and parallel to the strike of the fault."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla-inversa-frente-de-cabalgamiento","prefLabel":{"es":"falla inversa; frente de cabalgamiento","en":"reverse fault; thrust front"},"definition":{"es":"Falla en la que el bloque superior se ha desplazado hacia arriba respecto al bloque inferior; cuando el ángulo es bajo se denomina cabalgamiento.","en":"A fault in which the hanging wall has moved upward relative to the footwall; when the angle is low it is called a thrust."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla-normal-con-indicacion-de-labio-hundido","prefLabel":{"es":"falla normal con indicación de labio hundido","en":"normal fault with downthrown side indication"},"definition":{"es":"Falla en la que el bloque superior se ha desplazado hacia abajo respecto al bloque inferior, con indicación del labio hundido.","en":"A fault in which the hanging wall has moved downward relative to the footwall, with indication of the downthrown side."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla-supuesta","prefLabel":{"es":"falla supuesta","en":"inferred fault"},"definition":{"es":"Falla cuya existencia se deduce de evidencias indirectas pero no se ha observado directamente.","en":"A fault whose existence is inferred from indirect evidence but has not been directly observed."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/flexion-monoclinal","prefLabel":{"es":"flexión monoclinal","en":"monoclinal flexure"},"definition":{"es":"Inflexión o cambio de buzamiento en capas que forman un relieve monoclinal.","en":"An inflection or change in dip in layers forming a monoclinal relief."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/frente-montanyoso-lineal","prefLabel":{"es":"frente montañoso lineal","en":"linear mountain front"},"definition":{"es":"Frente montañoso de trazado rectilíneo controlado por una falla o estructura tectónica.","en":"A mountain front with a rectilinear trace controlled by a fault or tectonic structure."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/linea-de-capa-con-indicacion-de-buzamiento","prefLabel":{"es":"línea de capa con indicación de buzamiento","en":"bedding trace with dip indication"},"definition":{"es":"Traza de una capa sedimentaria en superficie con indicación del ángulo de buzamiento.","en":"Trace of a sedimentary bed at the surface with indication of the dip angle."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-conforme-anticlinal-mont","prefLabel":{"es":"relieve conforme anticlinal; mont","en":"anticlinal conform relief; mont"},"definition":{"es":"Relieve positivo cuya morfología coincide con la forma de un anticlinal subyacente.","en":"Positive relief whose morphology coincides with the shape of an underlying anticline."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-conforme-sinclinal-val","prefLabel":{"es":"relieve conforme sinclinal; val","en":"synclinal conform relief; val"},"definition":{"es":"Relieve negativo cuya morfología coincide con la forma de un sinclinal subyacente.","en":"Negative relief whose morphology coincides with the shape of an underlying syncline."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-invertido","prefLabel":{"es":"relieve invertido","en":"inverted relief"},"definition":{"es":"Relieve en el que las formas topográficas son opuestas a la estructura geológica subyacente.","en":"Relief in which the topographic forms are opposite to the underlying geological structure."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-de-capas-subverticales","prefLabel":{"es":"resalte de capas subverticales","en":"ledge of subvertical layers"},"definition":{"es":"Saliente rocoso formado por capas subverticales resistentes.","en":"A rock ledge formed by resistant subvertical layers."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-de-diques","prefLabel":{"es":"resalte de diques","en":"dyke ridge"},"definition":{"es":"Resalte topográfico causado por erosión diferencial de un dique volcánico resistente.","en":"A topographic ridge caused by differential erosion of a resistant volcanic dyke."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-en-capas-horizontales","prefLabel":{"es":"resalte en capas horizontales","en":"ledge in horizontal layers"},"definition":{"es":"Saliente rocoso en capas horizontales que forma un escalón en la topografía.","en":"A rock ledge in horizontal layers forming a step in the topography."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-en-capas-inclinadas-chevrons","prefLabel":{"es":"resalte en capas inclinadas; chevrons","en":"inclined layer ledge; chevrons"},"definition":{"es":"Resalte topográfico en capas inclinadas que presenta formas en V o chevron.","en":"A topographic ledge in inclined layers displaying V-shapes or chevron patterns."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/rumbo-e-inclinacion-o-buzamiento","prefLabel":{"es":"rumbo e inclinación o buzamiento","en":"strike and dip"},"definition":{"es":"Representación de la orientación de una capa o estructura planar mediante su rumbo y buzamiento.","en":"Representation of the orientation of a bed or planar structure by its strike and dip."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-estructural-degradada","prefLabel":{"es":"superficie estructural degradada","en":"degraded structural surface"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie estructural cuya forma original ha sido modificada por procesos erosivos.","en":"A structural surface whose original form has been modified by erosional processes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-estructural-exhumada","prefLabel":{"es":"superficie estructural (exhumada)","en":"exhumed structural surface"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie de un estrato resistente expuesta por erosión de los materiales suprayacentes.","en":"A resistant stratum surface exposed by erosion of overlying materials."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-subestructural-terminal","prefLabel":{"es":"superficie subestructural (terminal)","en":"substructural surface"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie erosiva desarrollada próxima y subparalela a un estrato resistente subyacente.","en":"An erosional surface developed close to and subparallel to an underlying resistant stratum."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/valle-de-fractura","prefLabel":{"es":"valle de fractura","en":"fracture valley"},"definition":{"es":"Valle excavado a favor de una zona de fractura o falla.","en":"A valley carved along a fracture zone or fault."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/zona-intensamente-fracturada","prefLabel":{"es":"zona intensamente fracturada","en":"intensely fractured zone"},"definition":{"es":"Zona con una densidad muy elevada de fracturas que condiciona la morfología del terreno.","en":"A zone with a very high density of fractures that conditions the terrain morphology."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-volcanicos","prefLabel":{"es":"objetos volcánicos","en":"volcanic features"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a procesos ígneos en virtud de los cuales magma y gases asociados atraviesan la corteza y son expulsados sobre la superficie terrestre y a la atmósfera.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to the deep seated (igneous) processes by which magma and associated gases rise through the crust and are extruded onto the earth's surface and into the atmosphere."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/bombas-bloques-erraticos","prefLabel":{"es":"bombas; bloques erráticos","en":"volcanic bombs; erratic blocks"},"definition":{"es":"Fragmentos de lava de gran tamaño expulsados durante una erupción volcánica.","en":"Large lava fragments expelled during a volcanic eruption."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-caldera","prefLabel":{"es":"borde de caldera","en":"caldera rim"},"definition":{"es":"Borde topográfico que delimita una caldera volcánica.","en":"The topographic rim that delimits a volcanic caldera."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-caldera-degradado","prefLabel":{"es":"borde de caldera degradado","en":"degraded caldera rim"},"definition":{"es":"Borde de caldera volcánica parcialmente destruido por erosión.","en":"A volcanic caldera rim partially destroyed by erosion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-crater-de-explosion-hidro-magmatica-con-anillo-de-toba-conservado","prefLabel":{"es":"borde de cráter de explosión hidro-magmática con anillo de toba conservado","en":"hydromagmatic explosion crater rim with preserved tuff ring"},"definition":{"es":"Borde de cráter de maar con anillo de tobas piroclásticas conservado.","en":"Maar crater rim with a preserved ring of pyroclastic tuffs."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-cenizas","prefLabel":{"es":"campo de cenizas","en":"ash field"},"definition":{"es":"Zona cubierta por cenizas volcánicas.","en":"An area covered by volcanic ash."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/centro-de-emision","prefLabel":{"es":"centro de emisión","en":"emission centre"},"definition":{"es":"Punto o zona desde donde se produce la emisión de material volcánico.","en":"A point or zone from which volcanic material is emitted."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/chimenea","prefLabel":{"es":"chimenea","en":"volcanic chimney"},"definition":{"es":"Conducto vertical por el que asciende el magma hasta la superficie.","en":"A vertical conduit through which magma rises to the surface."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cicatriz-de-deslizamiento-inducido-por-actividad-volcanica","prefLabel":{"es":"cicatriz de deslizamiento inducido por actividad volcánica","en":"volcano-induced landslide scar"},"definition":{"es":"Cicatriz de un deslizamiento provocado por actividad volcánica.","en":"Scar of a landslide caused by volcanic activity."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-de-lava","prefLabel":{"es":"colada de lava","en":"lava flow"},"definition":{"es":"Masa de lava que fluye o ha fluido sobre la superficie del terreno.","en":"A mass of lava that flows or has flowed over the ground surface."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-de-lava-lineal-salideros-lavicos","prefLabel":{"es":"colada de lava lineal; salideros lávicos","en":"linear lava flow; lava outbreak"},"definition":{"es":"Colada de lava de morfología lineal o salida lateral de lava.","en":"A lava flow with linear morphology or lateral lava outbreak."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-de-lava-tipo-aa-con-bloques-y-escorias-malpais","prefLabel":{"es":"colada de lava tipo aa; con bloques y escorias; malpaís","en":"aa lava flow; malpais"},"definition":{"es":"Colada de lava de superficie rugosa con bloques y escorias.","en":"A lava flow with a rough surface of blocks and scoriae."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-de-lava-tipo-pahoehoe-lava-cordada","prefLabel":{"es":"colada de lava tipo pahoehoe; lava cordada","en":"pahoehoe lava flow; ropy lava"},"definition":{"es":"Colada de lava de superficie lisa con morfología cordada.","en":"A lava flow with a smooth surface and ropy morphology."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-masiva-con-superficie-lisa","prefLabel":{"es":"colada masiva con superficie lisa","en":"massive lava flow with smooth surface"},"definition":{"es":"Colada de lava compacta con superficie lisa y homogénea.","en":"A compact lava flow with a smooth and homogeneous surface."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-meteorizada-o-degradada","prefLabel":{"es":"colada meteorizada o degradada","en":"weathered or degraded lava flow"},"definition":{"es":"Colada de lava cuya superficie ha sido alterada por meteorización.","en":"A lava flow whose surface has been altered by weathering."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-piroclastos","prefLabel":{"es":"cono de piroclastos","en":"pyroclastic cone"},"definition":{"es":"Edificio volcánico formado por acumulación de piroclastos alrededor de un centro de emisión.","en":"A volcanic edifice formed by accumulation of pyroclastic material around an emission centre."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-piroclastos-alomado-cabezo","prefLabel":{"es":"cono de piroclastos alomado; cabezo","en":"rounded pyroclastic cone"},"definition":{"es":"Cono de piroclastos con forma redondeada por degradación avanzada.","en":"A pyroclastic cone with a rounded shape due to advanced degradation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-piroclastos-degradado-con-centro-de-emision","prefLabel":{"es":"cono de piroclastos degradado con centro de emisión","en":"degraded pyroclastic cone with emission centre"},"definition":{"es":"Cono de piroclastos cuya morfología ha sido degradada por erosión, conservando el centro de emisión.","en":"A pyroclastic cone whose morphology has been degraded by erosion, preserving the emission centre."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-volcanico-con-crater","prefLabel":{"es":"cono volcánico con cráter","en":"volcanic cone with crater"},"definition":{"es":"Edificio volcánico cónico que conserva su cráter en la cima.","en":"A conical volcanic edifice that preserves its summit crater."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater","prefLabel":{"es":"cráter","en":"crater"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión circular o subcircular en la cima de un edificio volcánico.","en":"A circular or subcircular depression at the summit of a volcanic edifice."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-activo","prefLabel":{"es":"cráter activo","en":"active crater"},"definition":{"es":"Cráter volcánico con actividad fumarólica, sísmica o eruptiva actual.","en":"A volcanic crater with current fumarolic, seismic or eruptive activity."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-con-lago","prefLabel":{"es":"cráter con lago","en":"crater lake"},"definition":{"es":"Cráter volcánico que contiene un lago.","en":"A volcanic crater containing a lake."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-inactivo","prefLabel":{"es":"cráter inactivo","en":"inactive crater"},"definition":{"es":"Cráter volcánico sin actividad actual.","en":"A volcanic crater without current activity."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-de-domo-colada","prefLabel":{"es":"cráter de domo-colada","en":"dome-flow crater"},"definition":{"es":"Cráter asociado a un domo volcánico y sus coladas asociadas.","en":"A crater associated with a volcanic dome and its associated flows."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-de-explosion","prefLabel":{"es":"cráter de explosión","en":"explosion crater"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión circular o subcircular producida por una explosión volcánica.","en":"A circular or subcircular depression produced by a volcanic explosion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/depresion-intralavica","prefLabel":{"es":"depresión intralávica","en":"intralava depression"},"definition":{"es":"Depresión formada dentro de una colada de lava por colapso o deflación.","en":"A depression formed within a lava flow by collapse or deflation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/direccion-de-flujo-de-lava","prefLabel":{"es":"dirección de flujo de lava","en":"lava flow direction"},"definition":{"es":"Indicación de la dirección de movimiento de una colada de lava.","en":"Indication of the direction of movement of a lava flow."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/disyuncion-columnar","prefLabel":{"es":"disyunción columnar","en":"columnar jointing"},"definition":{"es":"Fracturación en columnas prismáticas de rocas volcánicas por enfriamiento.","en":"Prismatic columnar fracturing of volcanic rocks due to cooling."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo","prefLabel":{"es":"domo","en":"dome"},"definition":{"es":"Elevación redondeada formada por extrusión de lava viscosa.","en":"A rounded elevation formed by extrusion of viscous lava."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-endogeno","prefLabel":{"es":"domo endógeno","en":"endogenous dome"},"definition":{"es":"Domo volcánico formado por inyección de magma que levanta las capas superficiales.","en":"A volcanic dome formed by magma injection that uplifts surface layers."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-exogeno","prefLabel":{"es":"domo exógeno","en":"exogenous dome"},"definition":{"es":"Domo volcánico formado por extrusión de lava en superficie.","en":"A volcanic dome formed by lava extrusion at the surface."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-volcanico","prefLabel":{"es":"domo volcánico","en":"dome"},"definition":{"es":"Elevación redondeada formada por extrusión de lava viscosa.","en":"A rounded elevation formed by extrusion of viscous lava."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-frente-de-colada","prefLabel":{"es":"escarpe; frente de colada","en":"scarp; lava flow front"},"definition":{"es":"Frente o borde abrupto de una colada de lava.","en":"The front or abrupt edge of a lava flow."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fisura","prefLabel":{"es":"fisura","en":"fissure"},"definition":{"es":"Fractura abierta en un edificio volcánico por la que puede producirse emisión de lava o gases.","en":"An open fracture in a volcanic edifice through which lava or gases may be emitted."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fisura-con-fumarola-emergente","prefLabel":{"es":"fisura con fumarola emergente","en":"fissure with active fumarole"},"definition":{"es":"Fractura volcánica con emisión activa de gases y vapor.","en":"A volcanic fracture with active gas and steam emission."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fuente-termal","prefLabel":{"es":"fuente termal","en":"thermal spring"},"definition":{"es":"Manantial de agua calentada por actividad geotérmica.","en":"A spring of water heated by geothermal activity."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/geiser","prefLabel":{"es":"geiser","en":"geyser"},"definition":{"es":"Fuente termal que emite periódicamente chorros de agua caliente y vapor.","en":"A thermal spring that periodically emits jets of hot water and steam."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/gruta-jameo","prefLabel":{"es":"gruta; jameo","en":"grotto; jameo"},"definition":{"es":"Cavidad de origen volcánico, frecuentemente asociada a un tubo de lava colapsado.","en":"A cavity of volcanic origin, frequently associated with a collapsed lava tube."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hornito","prefLabel":{"es":"hornito","en":"hornito"},"definition":{"es":"Pequeño montículo de lava proyectada formado sobre una colada.","en":"A small mound of ejected lava formed on a flow."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hundimiento-subsidencia","prefLabel":{"es":"hundimiento; subsidencia","en":"collapse; subsidence"},"definition":{"es":"Descenso del terreno por colapso o subsidencia de origen volcánico.","en":"Ground lowering by collapse or subsidence of volcanic origin."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/meteorizacion-fumarolica","prefLabel":{"es":"meteorización fumarólica","en":"fumarolic weathering"},"definition":{"es":"Alteración de la roca volcánica por acción de gases fumarólicos.","en":"Alteration of volcanic rock by fumarolic gas action."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/muro-o-dique-lateral-de-enfriamiento-levee","prefLabel":{"es":"muro o dique lateral de enfriamiento; levée","en":"lateral cooling levee"},"definition":{"es":"Dique lateral formado por enfriamiento del borde de una colada de lava.","en":"A lateral dyke formed by cooling of the edge of a lava flow."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ojivas-de-presion","prefLabel":{"es":"ojivas de presión","en":"pressure ridges"},"definition":{"es":"Crestas arqueadas en la superficie de una colada de lava causadas por presión interna.","en":"Arched ridges on a lava flow surface caused by internal pressure."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/piton-aguja-necks","prefLabel":{"es":"pitón; aguja; necks","en":"volcanic plug; neck"},"definition":{"es":"Masa de lava solidificada en el interior de la chimenea volcánica expuesta por erosión.","en":"A mass of solidified lava in the volcanic chimney exposed by erosion."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-de-diques","prefLabel":{"es":"resalte de diques","en":"dyke ridge"},"definition":{"es":"Resalte topográfico causado por erosión diferencial de un dique volcánico resistente.","en":"A topographic ridge caused by differential erosion of a resistant volcanic dyke."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-de-diques-volcanico","prefLabel":{"es":"resalte de diques volcánico","en":"dyke ridge"},"definition":{"es":"Resalte topográfico causado por erosión diferencial de un dique volcánico resistente.","en":"A topographic ridge caused by differential erosion of a resistant volcanic dyke."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ruptura-de-pendiente-cascada-en-colada","prefLabel":{"es":"ruptura de pendiente; cascada en colada","en":"slope break; lava cascade"},"definition":{"es":"Cambio brusco de pendiente en una colada de lava.","en":"An abrupt slope change in a lava flow."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ruptura-de-pendiente-debido-a-reflejos-de-antiguos-bordes-de-crateres","prefLabel":{"es":"ruptura de pendiente debido a reflejos de antiguos bordes de cráteres","en":"slope break due to ancient crater rim remnants"},"definition":{"es":"Cambio de pendiente asociado a restos de antiguos bordes de cráteres volcánicos.","en":"Slope change associated with remnants of ancient volcanic crater rims."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-apilamiento-con-indicacion-de-inclinacion-de-la-misma","prefLabel":{"es":"superficie de apilamiento con indicación de inclinación de la misma","en":"stacking surface with dip indication"},"definition":{"es":"Superficie de contacto entre coladas o unidades volcánicas apiladas con indicación de su inclinación.","en":"Contact surface between stacked lava flows or volcanic units with dip indication."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/surgencia-lavica-bajo-colada-solidificada","prefLabel":{"es":"surgencia lávica bajo colada solidificada","en":"lava upwelling beneath solidified flow"},"definition":{"es":"Salida de lava fluida bajo la costra solidificada de una colada.","en":"Fluid lava emerging beneath the solidified crust of a flow."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/trazas-resaltes-de-capas-en-apilamientos-volcanicos-inclinados","prefLabel":{"es":"trazas, resaltes de capas en apilamientos volcánicos inclinados","en":"layer traces in inclined volcanic stacks"},"definition":{"es":"Resaltes topográficos de capas en secuencias volcánicas inclinadas.","en":"Topographic ledges of layers in inclined volcanic sequences."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/trazas-resaltes-de-capas-en-apilamientos-volcanicos-subhorizontales","prefLabel":{"es":"trazas, resaltes de capas en apilamientos volcánicos subhorizontales","en":"layer traces in subhorizontal volcanic stacks"},"definition":{"es":"Resaltes topográficos de capas en secuencias volcánicas subhorizontales.","en":"Topographic ledges of layers in subhorizontal volcanic sequences."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/tunel-de-lava","prefLabel":{"es":"túnel de lava","en":"lava tube"},"definition":{"es":"Conducto subterráneo formado por el flujo de lava bajo una costra solidificada.","en":"An underground conduit formed by lava flowing beneath a solidified crust."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/volcan-de-barro","prefLabel":{"es":"volcán de barro","en":"mud volcano"},"definition":{"es":"Estructura formada por emisión de barro, agua y gases a la superficie.","en":"A structure formed by the emission of mud, water and gases at the surface."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/volcan-de-barro-con-deposito-fangoso","prefLabel":{"es":"volcán de barro con depósito fangoso","en":"mud volcano with mud deposit"},"definition":{"es":"Volcán de barro con acumulación visible de depósitos fangosos.","en":"A mud volcano with visible accumulation of muddy deposits."}}]}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion","prefLabel":{"es":"superficie de erosión","en":"erosion surface"},"definition":{"es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados predominantemente con la erosión del agua, con exclusión de las corrientes canalizadas perennes (es decir, fluviales, glaciofluviales), o a la erosión eólica.","en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related dominantly to water erosion but excluding perennial channel flow (i.e. fluvial, glaciofluvial) or eolian erosion."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico","prefLabel":{"es":"cerro cónico","en":"conical hill"},"definition":{"es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica.","en":"A conical terrain elevation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico-poligenetico","prefLabel":{"es":"cerro cónico poligenético","en":"conical hill"},"definition":{"es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica.","en":"A conical terrain elevation."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-ruiniforme-caos-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"es":"cerro ruiniforme poligenetico","en":"ruiniform hill; block chaos"},"altLabel":{"es":["caos de bloques"]},"definition":{"es":"Relieve con aspe